@startuml
title LeMail - Status update and after-commit handoff
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam dpi 150
actor Shipper
participant "Rate limiter" as Limit
participant "JWT / controller" as API
participant ParcelsService as Service
participant StateMachineService as SM
database PostgreSQL as DB
participant TrackingGateway as WS
actor Customer
Shipper -> Limit : PATCH /api/parcels/{id}/status
alt quota exceeded
  Limit --> Shipper : 429 + Retry-After
else quota available
  Limit -> API : next
  API -> API : verify JWT
  API -> Service : updateStatus(id, dto, actor, userId)
  Service -> DB : read parcel
  Service -> SM : assertTransition(status, event, actor, dto)
  note right of SM
    Main still trusts client context.
    B02 must derive guard data from DB
    and verify owner / assignment.
  end note
  alt invalid actor / transition / guard
    SM --> API : 400 / 403
    API --> Shipper : rejected
  else valid
    SM --> Service : next status
    Service -> DB : BEGIN; UPDATE parcel; INSERT history
    alt write fails
      DB --> Service : rollback / error
      Service --> API : error, no emit
    else commit succeeds
      DB --> Service : updated parcel + history
      Service -> WS : emitStatusUpdated(snapshot)
      WS --> Customer : parcel.status.updated
      opt DELIVERED
        WS --> Customer : parcel.delivery.completed
      end
      Service --> API : updated parcel
      API --> Shipper : 200
    end
  end
end
note over Service,WS
  B02 replaces direct gateway call with onTransition after commit
  for create, initial assignment and later status changes.
  B03 sends the signed HTTP webhook through the same notifier.
  These integrations are pending, not accepted by this diagram.
end note
@enduml
